; Two stages of the LPC lattice (stages i and i-1, i = 8, 6 or 4). For each sample it reads the forward value f
; from the machine above, and b(i-2) of the sample before from the machine below. It sends b(i) of the sample
; before up, and the new f down. Every 20 samples (one step) it reads ten coefficient cards, five for each stage,
; straight into the multiply routines: the sign word (ADD t or SUB t), the two jumps into the row of nine ADDs
; (one per digit of the coefficient), the final SFT, and the rounding half. In a step whose A is 0 the cards
; are four SFT 00 and a half of 0, the cards of k = 0, so every product is 0.
;
; A stage is p = k b, f = f - p, q = k f, b(i) = b(i-1) + q. k x is Horner over the coefficient's two digits:
; c = +x or -x, d2 ADDs of c, SFT 01, d1 ADDs of c, then half a unit away from zero and SFT 0L. The row of ADDs
; is cells 90-98, and it runs on into cell 99, which holds the way back that the JMP into it left there.
;
; Address Contents Label Opcode Operand Comment
  03            loop    OUT   bhi      03-07: b(i) of the sample before goes up; every 20 samples, new coefficients
  04                    CLA   cnt
  05                    SUB   00
  06                    STO   cnt
  07                    TAC   coef
  08            go      INP   f        08-17: stage i
  09                    CLA   blo
  10                    JMP   mulh
  11                    STO   p
  12                    CLA   f
  13                    SUB   p
  14                    STO   f
  15                    JMP   mulh
  16                    ADD   blo
  17                    STO   bhi
  18            getb    INP   bx       18-29: stage i-1, then f goes down
  19                    CLA   bx
  20                    JMP   mull
  21                    STO   p
  22                    CLA   f
  23                    SUB   p
  24                    STO   f
  25                    JMP   mull
  26                    ADD   bx
  27                    STO   blo
  28                    OUT   f
  29                    JMP   loop
  30            coef    CLA   n19      30-42: a step's ten coefficient cards
  31                    STO   cnt
  32                    INP   sh
  33                    INP   t1h
  34                    INP   t2h
  35                    INP   finh
  36                    INP   hh
  37                    INP   sl
  38                    INP   t1l
  39                    INP   t2l
  40                    INP   finl
  41                    INP   hl
  42                    JMP   go
  43            mulh    STO   t        43-58: k x for stage i, x in the accumulator
  44                    CLA   99
  45                    STO   reth
  46                    CLA   z
  47            sh      DATA  0        (ADD t or SUB t)
  48                    STO   c
  49                    CLA   z
  50            t1h     DATA  0        (JMP into the row, d2 ADDs)
  51                    SFT   01
  52            t2h     DATA  0        (JMP into the row, d1 ADDs)
  53                    TAC   negh
  54                    ADD   hh
  55            finh    DATA  0        (SFT 0L)
  56            reth    DATA  0
  57            negh    SUB   hh
  58                    JMP   finh
  59            mull    STO   t        59-84: k x for stage i-1
  60                    CLA   99
  61                    STO   retl
  62                    CLA   z
  63            sl      DATA  0
  64                    STO   c
  65                    CLA   z
  66            t1l     DATA  0
  67                    SFT   01
  68            t2l     DATA  0
  69                    TAC   negl
  70                    ADD   hl
  71            finl    DATA  0
  72            retl    DATA  0
  73            negl    SUB   hl
  74                    JMP   finl
  75            hh      DATA  0
  76            hl      DATA  0
  77            z       DATA  0
  78            p       DATA  0
  79            f       DATA  0
  80            blo     DATA  0
  81            bhi     DATA  0
  82            bx      DATA  0
  83            cnt     DATA  0
  84            n19     DATA  19
  86            t       DATA  0        t and c are at the same cells in every lattice machine
  87            c       DATA  0
  90            row     ADD   c        90-98: the row of nine ADDs, into 99
  91                    ADD   c
  92                    ADD   c
  93                    ADD   c
  94                    ADD   c
  95                    ADD   c
  96                    ADD   c
  97                    ADD   c
  98                    ADD   c
